<title>BRAZIL: Brazil posts $170 mln trade gap in 1st wk of April.</title>
<headline>Brazil posts $170 mln trade gap in 1st wk of April.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil posted a trade deficit of $170 million in the first week of April, with exports of $808 million and imports totalling $978 million, the Industry and Commerce Ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that average daily exports were $202.1 million and average daily imports $244.5 million.</p>
<p>There were no comparative figures for the first week of April 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 5561 223 0358))</p>
